#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate the table/layout report from frozen benchmark and validation evidence."""
import json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'reports/multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
def main():
 s=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/summary.json');q=read(OUT/'quality-results.json');env=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/environment.json');c=read(OUT/'change-summary.json');v=read(OUT/'validation/summary.json')
 b=s['engines']['bulkparse'];a=s['engines']['anydoc'];prev=read(ROOT/'reports/multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12/benchmark-final/summary.json')
 previous={k:sum(q['cohorts'][co][k] for co in ['previous_45','additional_equations']) for k in ['before','after','anydoc','checks']}
 lines=['# Complex tables and layout — 12 November 2026','',
 'BulkParse-owned general rules improve **eight of the 62 previously partial outputs**. All 81 conversion inputs still return output. ODF table cells recover lists and nested tables, RTF uses physical cell boundaries and merge chains, spreadsheet covered-cell content no longer creates overlapping geometry, and positioned PPTX/ODP objects follow a conservative reading order. No document-specific branches or runtime AnyDoc/Docling dependencies were added.','',
 '## Selected quality checks','',
 '| Source-grounded checks | BulkParse before | BulkParse after | AnyDoc |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for name,r in [('Unchanged previous checks',previous),('New table content and layout',q['cohorts']['table_content_layout']),('Explicit nested-table / merge / header structure',q['cohorts']['table_structure'])]:lines.append(f"| {name} | {r['before']}/{r['checks']} | {r['after']}/{r['checks']} | {r['anydoc']}/{r['checks']} |")
 lines += [f"| Total | {q['totals']['before']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['after']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['anydoc']}/{q['checks']} |",'',
 '**These are selected development checks, not an independent test or a whole-document quality percentage.** The previous 54 predicates are unchanged. Fifteen new expectations were derived from source XML/control records. The three explicit-structure checks require semantic nested tables, spans and declared headers; AnyDoc’s expanded Markdown can retain their text/alignment while flattening that structure. They are reported separately to make this output-model difference visible.','',
 'All previously passing selected checks remain passing. AnyDoc’s three missed new content/layout expectations concern slide table/footnote and caption/image ordering; the older misses concern chartsheet content and spreadsheet comments. These results do not establish overall superiority or reproduce AnyDoc’s private 100-document LLM-judged benchmark.','',
 f"The status count remains **{c['statuses']['partial']} partial / {c['statuses']['complete']} complete**. Fixing a table does not remove unrelated image, style, numbering or auxiliary-story limitations. Partial diagnostics are preserved for unresolved features; complete status is not proof of perfect fidelity. All 62 baseline partial documents are covered in the [audit](partial-audit.md), including unchanged outputs.",'',
 '### Concrete changes','',
 '- **ODF cell content:** recursively retains paragraphs, lists, inline emphasis, explicit line breaks and nested tables. This restores whole list-only cells and the list-backed ODP slide table that previously had an empty grid. Explicit `table-header-rows` become semantic headers. Repeated cells have separately budgeted blocks and provenance.',
 '- **RTF table geometry:** unions declared left/right edges into shared columns, joins horizontal continuations, and matches vertical continuations only to a compatible immediately preceding chain. Unequal row boundaries produce appropriate spans. Orphan continuations keep their text and a diagnostic. Missing/non-increasing boundaries use a diagnosed fallback; nested RTF tables remain incomplete.',
 '- **Merged covered content:** nonempty covered cells join their anchor while retaining original block coordinates and supported styles. The XLSB example no longer extends a four-column grid with overlapping cells. Keeping this ambiguous stored content is deliberate and remains diagnosed; it is not proof that the hidden content should be visually shown.',
 '- **Slide ordering:** own or available inherited PPTX bounds and explicit ODP length units determine order within contiguous positioned groups. Near-aligned objects sort left-to-right using a band anchored at its first top edge. Unknown geometry creates an order barrier. Rotated/flipped PPTX groups and transformed ODP groups keep source order. Overlapping layouts, complex transforms and semantic multi-column reading order remain heuristic.',
 '- **Structured rendering:** rich cells use escaped HTML so lists, nested tables, headers and spans survive Markdown export. Plain tables still use GFM. Existing PDF fragment spacing is preserved; Office paragraph boundaries are not imposed on PDF text fragments. Consumers need HTML-table support for the richer output.',
 '- **PPTX tables:** cell text now uses the existing rich-text/list reader; declared grids, merge continuations and `firstRow` headers are preserved. Oversized or overlapping merges are bounded/rejected.',
 '- Legacy DOC/PPT table geometry, spreadsheet table-region metadata, full ODF cell-style cascade, images/SmartArt, complex charts and visual fidelity remain unfinished. This task does not resolve all 62 documents completely.','',
 'The [output review](output-change-review.json) covers all eight changed predictions: no prior word/number tokens disappear in its normalized token check, and all 32 emitted HTML tables have consistent rectangular occupancy. These are useful regression guards, not semantic proof for every cell. The previous XLSB output had inconsistent row extents; the new output does not.','',
 '## Same-machine benchmark','',
 f"Machine: **{env['machine']}**, {env['platform']}. BulkParse {env['versions']['bulkparse']} (schema **0.5**), AnyDoc {env['versions']['anydoc']}, Docling {env['versions']['docling']}. Corpus: the unchanged 70 upstream conversion fixtures plus 11 authored inputs; nine robustness inputs run separately.",'',
 '| Engine | Returned / attempted | Median sequential full-corpus time | Lifetime peak RSS |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for engine,r in s['engines'].items():lines.append(f"| {engine} | {r['returned']}/{r['attempted']} | {r['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms | {s['resources'][engine]['lifetime_peak_rss_bytes']/1048576:.1f} MiB |")
 runs={e:[read(OUT/f'benchmark-final/{e}-pass-{i}.json')['documents'] for i in range(1,6)] for e in s['engines']};common=set.intersection(*[{r['path'] for r in val[0] if r['ok']} for val in runs.values()]);times={e:statistics.median(sum(r['elapsed_ns'] for r in run if r['path'] in common)/1e6 for run in val) for e,val in runs.items()}
 lines += ['',
 'BulkParse and AnyDoc process the **identical 81 inputs**. Docling attempts only 31 supported OOXML inputs; six existing synthetic PPTX failures remain included in its attempted-corpus timings. On the same '+str(len(common))+' inputs returned by all three, medians are '+', '.join(f'{e} **{t:.3f} ms**' for e,t in times.items())+'.','',
 'Protocol: one excluded full warm-up followed by five rotating-engine-order full-corpus passes. Every worker processes documents sequentially in one persistent process with thread settings of one. Clocks include file reads, parsing and default Markdown export; they exclude startup, IPC, output serialization/writes and scoring. Corpus time is the sum of per-document clocks. Five-pass predictions/outcomes are deterministic. RSS is macOS process-lifetime peak, including warm-up and the Rust workers’ separate robustness pass; it is not incremental memory per document. CPU resource logs include startup.','',
 f"Previous BulkParse run: **{prev['engines']['bulkparse']['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms**, **{prev['resources']['bulkparse']['lifetime_peak_rss_bytes']/1048576:.1f} MiB**. Current BulkParse conversion time is **{b['median_corpus_ms']/a['median_corpus_ms']:.3f}× AnyDoc’s** on these inputs. The old/new measurements are separate runs, not interleaved binaries. Extra retained content and different output semantics affect the workload. Small macOS development fixtures do not establish Linux production throughput.",'',
 '| Format | Inputs | BulkParse median document ms | AnyDoc median document ms | BulkParse partial |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for fmt,eng in s['per_format'].items():
  bb=eng['bulkparse'];aa=eng['anydoc'];lines.append(f"| {fmt.upper()} | {bb['attempted']} | {bb['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {aa['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {bb['partial']} |")
 lines += ['', 'Per-document medians use five measurements, then aggregate by extension. Failed attempts stay in timing aggregates. XLSM is an alias, not a separate parser.','',
 '## Validation and design references','',
 f"- **{v['rust_all_tests']} all-feature Rust workspace tests pass**, including **44 Office integration tests** and one new ordering unit test. Minimal core: **{v['rust_minimal_tests']}**; Office-only: **{v['rust_office_tests']}**. Clippy with warnings denied and formatting checks pass.",
 '- Seven new integration tests plus the ordering unit test cover varying boundaries, merge chains/orphans, covered-cell styles/provenance, rich/nested cells and headers, ordering barriers, transformed groups, unit conversion and table limits. They use authored examples, not production filename checks.',
 '- Node/Python each pass four smoke tests; WASM smoke tests pass. Full JSON/Markdown parity: **27 conversions + three inspections** across Node, Python, WASM and CLI, including all eight changed upstream outputs. Extended parity: **34 conversions + three inspections** with `node --liftoff-only`.',
 '- The previously documented default Node 24 optimizing-compiler OOM on larger PDF/WASM cases remains unresolved. Extended parity used the known interpreter/baseline-compiler workaround; this is not a claim that default extended execution works. Linux/browser testing remains outstanding.',
 '- All **200 reference PDF Markdown predictions are byte-for-byte unchanged** using the benchmarked binary. PDF NID/TEDS/MHS scoring and speed were not rerun; this is a regression equality check for Office changes.',
 '- Existing authored semantic checks remain 11/11 for BulkParse and AnyDoc, 2/2 for Docling. The nine separate robustness outcomes remain unchanged: BulkParse rejects eight and recovers one RTF; AnyDoc rejects seven and recovers that RTF plus one damaged-persistence PPT. BulkParse’s recovered malformed RTF now exports its declared wide header correctly; its nested table remains flattened and diagnosed.','',
 'AnyDoc’s RTF edge-based grid and continuation handling informed the independent table builder. Docling’s position-based slide iteration informed ordering; BulkParse uses relative-height bands without transitive chaining and preserves unknown positions as barriers. These concepts were implemented in BulkParse’s own document model, limits and renderer. Exact reviewed-file hashes are in [design-reference-hashes.json](design-reference-hashes.json), with notices in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Production rules use format properties, coordinates and relationships; benchmark filenames/text appear only in test/evaluation code.','',
 '## Reproduce and download','',
 'Restore the hash-matched corpora and comparator environments described in the [multiformat protocol](../../benchmarks/multiformat/README.md).','',
 '```sh','cargo test --workspace --all-features','cargo build --release -p bulkparse --example office_bench','python3 scripts/benchmark_office_formats.py --out reports/my-table-run','python3 scripts/validate_office_benchmark.py reports/my-table-run','python3 scripts/evaluate_office_quality.py --run reports/my-table-run \\','  --baseline reports/multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12/benchmark-final \\','  --spec reports/multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12/quality-checks.json \\','  --out reports/my-table-evaluation','python3 scripts/audit_table_layout_outputs.py --run reports/my-table-run \\','  --out reports/my-table-evaluation/output-change-review.json','python3 scripts/check_office_pdf_regression.py --out reports/my-table-evaluation/pdf-regression.json','```','',
 '- [Download source and evidence ZIP](../multiformat-tables-layout-2026-11-12.zip). Upstream documents, dependencies and compiled binaries are excluded.',
 '- [Benchmark summary](benchmark-final/summary.json), [environment and binary hashes](benchmark-final/environment.json), [corpus manifest](benchmark-final/manifest.json), [source hashes](benchmark-final/source-manifest.json).',
 '- [Quality manifest](quality-checks.json), [all check outcomes](quality-results.json), [62-document partial audit](partial-audit.md), [validation](validation/summary.json), [PDF equality](pdf-regression.json).',
 '- Raw warm-up and five-pass outputs, complete predictions, resource logs and robustness outcomes are under `benchmark-final`; `before-source` and `source-snapshot` preserve the previous and final implementation.',
 '- [Previous report](../multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12/README.md).','']
 (OUT/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
